{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-32647" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/state.json" "file_sha256" "385e6f069156dc0f6f898e7f6f18862954ab6b167731863a03f1cd8b297536db"} {"question" "q-32647" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=2 \\\\ -4{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=2$ and ${y}_{2}=6.$ \n\nTherefore, $y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/state.json" "file_sha256" "385e6f069156dc0f6f898e7f6f18862954ab6b167731863a03f1cd8b297536db"} {"question" "q-32647" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0a855bb07bf8dede1768bc415331b9700f0c7b9e0347f38a6be52438ac7df5f3"} {"question" "q-32647" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/state.json" "file_sha256" "385e6f069156dc0f6f898e7f6f18862954ab6b167731863a03f1cd8b297536db"} {"question" "q-32647" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/state.json" "file_sha256" "385e6f069156dc0f6f898e7f6f18862954ab6b167731863a03f1cd8b297536db"} {"question" "q-32647" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/state.json" "file_sha256" "385e6f069156dc0f6f898e7f6f18862954ab6b167731863a03f1cd8b297536db"} {"question" "q-107172" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/state.json" "file_sha256" "385e6f069156dc0f6f898e7f6f18862954ab6b167731863a03f1cd8b297536db"} {"question" "q-107172" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=0 \\\\ -6{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=0$ and ${y}_{2}=4.$ \n\nTherefore, $y=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/state.json" "file_sha256" "385e6f069156dc0f6f898e7f6f18862954ab6b167731863a03f1cd8b297536db"} {"question" "q-107172" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0a855bb07bf8dede1768bc415331b9700f0c7b9e0347f38a6be52438ac7df5f3"} {"question" "q-107172" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/state.json" "file_sha256" "385e6f069156dc0f6f898e7f6f18862954ab6b167731863a03f1cd8b297536db"} {"question" "q-107172" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "y=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "y=[\\be