file_sha256" "385e6f069156dc0f6f898e7f6f18862954ab6b167731863a03f1cd8b297536db"} {"question" "q-107171" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=5 \\\\ -7{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this system is ${y}_{1}=5$ and ${y}_{2}=33.$ \n\nTherefore, $y=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 33\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/state.json" "file_sha256" "385e6f069156dc0f6f898e7f6f18862954ab6b167731863a03f1cd8b297536db"} {"question" "q-107171" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0a855bb07bf8dede1768bc415331b9700f0c7b9e0347f38a6be52438ac7df5f3"} {"question" "q-107171" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/state.json" "file_sha256" "385e6f069156dc0f6f898e7f6f18862954ab6b167731863a03f1cd8b297536db"} {"question" "q-107171" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "y=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "y=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 33\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "y=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/state.json" "file_sha256" "385e6f069156dc0f6f898e7f6f18862954ab6b167731863a03f1cd8b297536db"} {"question" "q-107171" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 33\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/state.json" "file_sha256" "385e6f069156dc0f6f898e7f6f18862954ab6b167731863a03f1cd8b297536db"} {"question" "q-107174" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -4 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/state.json" "file_sha256" "385e6f069156dc0f6f898e7f6f18862954ab6b167731863a03f1cd8b297536db"} {"question" "q-107174" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=-2 \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=-1 \\\\ -{y}_{1}-4{y}_{2}+{y}_{3}=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the solution to this system using forward substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =-2, \\\\ {y}_{2} & =-1-{y}_{1} \\\\  & =-1-(-2) \\\\  & =1, \\\\ {y}_{3} & =-3+4{y}_{2}+{y}_{1} \\\\  & =-3+4(1)+(-2) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$y=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/state.json" "file_sha256" "385e6f069156dc0f6f898e7f6f18862954ab6b167731863a03f1cd8b297536db"} {"question" "q-107174" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0a855bb07bf8dede1768bc415331b9700f0c7b9e0347f38a6be52438ac7df5f3"} {"question" "q-107174" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/state.json" "file_sha256" "385e6f069156dc0f6f898e7f6f18862954ab6b167731863a03f1cd8b297536db"} {"question" "q-107174" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "y=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "y=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/state.json" "file_sha256" "385e6f069156dc0f6f898e7f6f18862954ab6b167731863a03f1cd8b297536db"} {"question" "q-107174" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/state.json" "file_sha256" "385e6f069156dc0f6f898e7f6f18862954ab6b167731863a03f1cd8b297536db"} {"question" "q-105928" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/state.json" "file_sha256" "385e6f069156dc0f6f898e7f6f18862954ab6b167731863a03f1cd8b297536db"} {"question" "q-105928" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=-7 \\\\ -{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=3 \\\\ 3{y}_{2}+{y}_{3}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the solution to this system using forward substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =-7, \\\\ {y}_{2} & =3+{y}_{1} \\\\  & =3+(-7) \\\\  & =-4, \\\\ {y}_{3} & =3-3{y}_{2} \\\\  & =3-3(-4) \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$y=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/state.json" "file_sha256" "385e6f069156dc0f6f898e7f6f18862954ab6b167731863a03f1cd8b297536db"} {"question" "q-105928" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0a855bb07bf8dede1768bc415331b9700f0c7b9e0347f38a6be52438ac7df5f3"} {"question" "q-105928" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/state.json" "file_sha256" "385e6f069156dc0f6f898e7f6f18862954ab6b167731863a03f1cd8b297536db"} {"question" "q-105928" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "y=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "y=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "y=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "y=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/state.json" "file_sha256" "385e6f069156dc0f6f898e7f6f18862954ab6b167731863a03f1cd8b297536db"} {"question" "q-105928" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/state.json" "file_sha256" "385e6f069156dc0f6f898e7f6f18862954ab6b167731863a03f1cd8b297536db"} {"question" "q-105934" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $L$ and the vector $b,$ given by \n\n$$\nL=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU factorization of some $3\\times 3$ matrix $A,$ find the vector $y$ such that\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to $Ax=b.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063081/state.json" "file_sha256" "385e6f069156dc0f6f898e7f6f18862954ab6b167731863a03f1cd8b297536db"} {"question" "q-105934" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that since $A=LU,$ we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax=b\\,⟹\\,{{(LU)}_{⏟}}_{A}x=b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, setting $Ux=y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nL{{(Ux)}_{⏟}}_{y}=b\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}Ly=b \\\\ Ux=y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now solve $Ly=b.$ Writing this equation in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives the system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=9 \\\\ 7{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}=7 \\\\ -9{y}_{1}+{y}_{3}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the solution to this system using forward substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & =9, \\\\ {y}_{2} & =7-7{y}_{1} \\\\  & =7-7(9) \\\\  & =-56, \\\\ {y}_{3} & =-1+9{y}_{1} \\\\  & =-1+9(9) \\\\  & =80.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$y=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -56 \\\\ 80\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers